/* The two prompts iOS draws itself, in its own dialog, before Eter can say
   anything. They are the only user-facing copy in this product that does not
   come from `core/i18n/` — the system owns the sentence, and it reads whichever
   localisation matches the *device* language. */

"NSMicrophoneUsageDescription" = "Eter uses the microphone only while you are speaking a journal entry, and only when you start it.";
"NSSpeechRecognitionUsageDescription" = "Speech is turned into text so you can speak a journal entry instead of typing it. Only the transcript is kept.";
